KS-764: Peter's three lines and a fixture — loopback binds, the export-presence control, the no-tenant refusal pinned on both routes

Answers PR #799 review 5153121542 / comment 5600549339 at the current head, after develop `8861e6216` was merged in (the previous commit).

Item 1 — loopback (2 lines). `app.listen(0, cb)` puts the callback in the host slot and binds every interface; the packages/shared test-listener guard now on this branch reds both wire suites for it. Both sites read `app.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', cb)` — host second, callback last.
  - services/originate/src/__tests__/ks764-admin-api-keys-revoke-route-contract.test.ts (was :121)
  - services/security/src/__tests__/ks764-revoke-organisation-route-contract.test.ts (was :128)
  Red-first on the merged tree before the edit: the guard's red cell `1 failed | 22 passed (23)`, naming exactly those two paths and no other; after: `23 passed (23)`.

Item 2 — F-2 (1 line). `expect(typeof shared.decideKeyRevoke).toBe('function')` is now the FIRST assertion of the originate CONTROL cell. Measured with the export deleted from packages/shared/dist/index.js (the stale-dist state Peter cited): without this line the cell is GREEN — `jest.isMockFunction(undefined)` is false and `undefined === undefined` — exactly his claim; with it, RED (`Expected "function" / Received "undefined"`).

Item 3 — F-3 (1 fixture, on BOTH routes). A principal naming its organisation but carrying NO tenant claim (`ADMIN_NO_TENANT`) revoking an org-owned key:
  - originate CASE 5: 403 FORBIDDEN, the pre-flight SELECT ran once, the refusal log carries `reason: 'caller has no tenant'` (the body is generic by KS-764's own design, so the arm is pinned via `logger.warn`, spied and calling through), and the UPDATE is not called.
  - security CASE 5: 403 FORBIDDEN, success false. Added here too because the ks742 suite's DELETE cells cover cross-tenant and the platform bypass only — its tenant-less cells are GET and POST.
  Red-first: with the policy's no-tenant arm tampered to allow (packages/shared rebuilt), originate `1 failed | 9 passed` (CASE 5: Expected 403, Received 200) and security `1 failed | 6 passed`; restored by content, sha-asserted, rebuilt, green. The security run also shows the route reaches the policy for a tenant-less caller — nothing earlier refuses it.
  The originate harness docblock now declares that the stub sets `req.tenantId` from the principal, which `authenticate()` does not (`extractTenantContext` does, in production), and that `logger.warn` is observed.

Tampers, each restored by content with the whole-file sha asserted; the shared tamper followed by a rebuild and a re-run:
  T1  originate bind reverted to `app.listen(0, () => resolve())`  -> guard red, exactly 1 path named            aimed 1, got 1
  T2  `decideKeyRevoke` export removed from packages/shared/dist     -> typeof line red; the old two lines green  aimed 1, got 1 (+6 CASE/PLATFORM cells 500 through the route — the consequence, not the aim)
  T3  policy no-tenant arm -> allow, rebuilt                          -> CASE 5 red on originate AND on security   aimed 1+1, got 1+1

Suites at this head (bash 3.2.57, node v24.7.0, darwin arm64): packages/shared 42 files 828/828 · services/security 16 files 205/205 · services/originate 56 suites 598/598 (the ks444 webhooks pair that read red at 38f6377b9 is fixed on develop and cleared by the merge) · services/api-gateway 34 files 343/343 (packages/shared's export surface is this PR's) · tsc --noEmit clean in originate and security.

Not addressed at this head, by name: Peter's 6(b)/6(c) (hardcoded 403 vs decision.status; two refusal texts) — backlog; his nit (200 {success:false} on the tenant-scoped miss) — left, as he said; the 09-04 pass's F-1 (request-derived tenant vs the key row's own) — on the record; the live 8-case matrix — his.

